#### 7. Exception Handling in Tests (Lines 110–118)

**Test:** `ProcessOrder_EmptyOrder_ThrowsValidationError`  
**Evidence:** Manual `try/catch` instead of `Assert.ThrowsException<T>`.

```csharp
try
{
    processor.ProcessOrder(order);
    Assert.Fail("Expected an exception...");
}
catch (ValidationException ex)
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Order must contain at least one item", ex.Message);
}
```

**Fix:**

```csharp
var ex = Assert.ThrowsException<ValidationException>(
    () => processor.ProcessOrder(order));
Assert.AreEqual("Order must contain at least one item", ex.Message);
```

**Risk:** If `Assert.Fail` is accidentally removed, the test silently passes on no-throw paths.

