## Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix Effort | Impact |
|----------|-------|-----------|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | Low (add assertions) | Eliminates false-pass |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | Low (split test) | Closes hidden gap |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | Medium (async refactor) | Removes flakiness + 2 s |
| 4 | Mystery Guest | Low (inline data) | Removes env coupling |
| 5 | Exception Handling | Low (use ThrowsException) | Cleaner, safer |
| 6 | Magic Number Test | Low (named constants) | Readability |
| 7 | Sensitive Equality | Medium (structural assert) | Reduces brittleness |
| 8 | Eager Test | Medium (split or tag) | Better diagnostics |
| 9 | General Fixture | Trivial (delete field) | Reduces noise |

All smell names above map directly to the **testsmells.org** academic catalog and are citable as such (Peruma et al., *TSE 2020*; van Deursen et al., *Refactoring Test Code*, XP 2001).
